WEBVTT

00:11:57.833 --> 00:12:00.268
I mean, power games are fascinating.

00:12:00.292 --> 00:12:01.559
Fascinating.

00:12:01.583 --> 00:12:02.851
AG: I think so, too.

00:12:02.875 --> 00:12:07.268
So I'm asking you this question
about our power dynamic

00:12:07.292 --> 00:12:09.893
in part because I think
it's a lens into understanding

00:12:09.917 --> 00:12:11.184
how you think about power.

00:12:11.208 --> 00:12:14.268
So when you say power shifts
back and forth in this conversation,

00:12:14.292 --> 00:12:16.143
how do you see it shifting?

00:12:16.167 --> 00:12:21.768
EP: So I think I am trying to grope --

00:12:21.792 --> 00:12:25.643
to reach for, I'm trying
to reach for places

00:12:25.667 --> 00:12:27.684
where I think, do you agree with me?

00:12:27.708 --> 00:12:29.059
Do you see what I'm saying?

00:12:29.083 --> 00:12:30.726
Can you build on what I'm saying?